.TH CCOL_CHAN_MSG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_msg_count \- get the current message count of a direction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

size_t ccol_chan_msg_count(ccol_channel *ch, ccol_channel_direction d);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives the number of messages that the queue of the given
direction holds now.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to ask
d    Direction to ask about (ccol_owner_to_workers or
     ccol_workers_to_owner)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The function gives the number of messages in the given direction.
It gives (size_t)-1 on an error. The ccol_channel is NULL, or the
direction is not valid.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The count is a thread-safe snapshot.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_recv_zc (3)
